# `tree-sitter build` writes the compiled parser next to the grammar as
# `carve.so` (`carve.dylib` on macOS), the same way `build --wasm` writes
# `carve.wasm` above. One of those got committed once and sat in the tree for
# three weeks; a compiled parser in the repository is a third copy that goes
# stale on its own schedule, alongside the shared `tree-sitter` libdir cache and
# the `bindings/node` addon, and a stale parser produces a plausible wrong tree
# rather than an error. `make` writes `lib*.so`/`lib*.dylib` here too.
*.so
*.dylib
